\title{Categorical Tropical Rips Interleaving: Interleaving Distance as
Tropical Algebra, with Rank and Shift Functoriality}

\author{The Catalog Bridges Project}
\date{2026-06-15}

\begin{document}

\begin{abstract}
We develop a self-contained, fully formalized bridge connecting three areas:
\emph{categorical persistence theory} (functors out of the ordered real line and
their interleavings), \emph{tropical / min-plus algebra} (the semiring
$\mathrm{Tropical}\,\Rext$ in which multiplication is ordinary addition and
addition is minimum), and \emph{geometry / topological data analysis}
(Vietoris--Rips filtrations of dissimilarities and their stability under
perturbation). Modeling persistence modules as monotone functors $M:\mathbb{R}\to
\alpha$ into a preorder, we define $\varepsilon$-interleavings as pairs of shifted
dominations and prove the categorical structure: reflexivity, symmetry, monotone
weakening, and the composition law ($\varepsilon$-interleaving followed by
$\delta$-interleaving is an $(\varepsilon+\delta)$-interleaving). We construct the
$\Rext$-valued \emph{interleaving distance} as an infimum of admissible shifts and
prove it is a pseudometric. Our central structural result is that the triangle
inequality is \emph{exactly} submultiplicativity of $\trop\circ\idist$ in
$\mathrm{Tropical}\,\Rext$. We instantiate the theory with Vietoris--Rips modules
and prove the \emph{stability theorem}. We then prove two functoriality results:
over a finite type the \emph{rank functor} $\rankMod:\PersMod(\mathrm{Set}\,\beta)
\to\PersMod\,\mathbb{N}$ preserves $\varepsilon$-interleavings and is
$1$-Lipschitz for the interleaving distance; and the \emph{constant-shift functor}
$\shift\,c$ is an isometry of the interleaving distance, displaces a module by at
most $c$, realizes the self-distance as the tropical multiplicative unit, and the
relation of finite interleaving distance is an equivalence relation equal to
$\idist\ne\top$. All results are formalized with zero unproven steps.
\end{abstract}

